# Keep cloud-init out of the live ISO. Its presence is the whole switch: cloud-init's
# systemd generator looks only for this path and never checks what is in it, so this text
# is for you, not for it.
#
# Why: the autoinstall drive is labeled `cidata` because that is the cloud-init NoCloud
# label and hypervisors already know how to attach one. The ISO reads that drive itself,
# with omarchy-cidata-load. cloud-init is not part of the feature -- but it ships in the
# Arch releng profile this ISO is seeded from, and its ds-identify sees the same label and
# concludes it has a NoCloud datasource to configure.
#
# What that costs, measured on a MacBookPro16,2 (boot id e32aa3be, 2026-09-19): cloud-init
# writes a fallback DHCP config for every interface it finds, including the T2's internal
# USB NCM Ethernet (enp230s0f1u1), which is not connected to anything and never gets a
# lease. systemd-networkd-wait-online --any then runs its full 120 s timeout, from 8.7 s to
# 128.7 s. cloud-init-network orders itself Before=systemd-user-sessions, so getty@tty1 and
# plymouth-quit wait behind it: autologin at 129.4 s for an install that takes 85-93 s. The
# machine is idle throughout -- 1.3% CPU, no iowait. It is pure waiting on a dead NIC.
